\title{Augmenting increases flow value}
\date{2026-11-12T18:11:52Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\taxon{Lemma}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{Augmenting along an #{s}-#{t} path in the residual network always \em{increases} the [value](00S0) of the flow in #{G}.}

\proof{Any #{s}-#{t} path in #{G_f} has to start along some outgoing
  edge from #{s}, which must be a "forwards" edge corresponding to an
  outgoing edge from #{s} in #{G}. So when we augment along the path
  we increase the flow along that edge, which [by definition](00S0) increases
  the value of the flow.}

